- public void solveSudoku(char[][] board)
- requires board != null && board.length == 9 && (\forall int i; 0 <= i && i < board.length; board[i].length == 9)
- ensures (\forall int i; 0 <= i && i < board.length; (\forall int j; 0 <= j && j < board[i].length; board[i][j] is a digit or '.' && board[i][j] != null))
- ensures the sudoku puzzle is solved correctly according to the rules mentioned above